// MiraVelo bike leasing: the real parts of this example and how we source them.
// Read it top-down: Customer, Back office and Operations at the top, commodities at the bottom right.
// Decorators: build = Make, buy = Buy a product, outsource = Buy as a service, market = Partner.
// No decorator = open decision. Annotations 1 to 4 name the open decisions, GitHub issues #8 to #11.
// Adapt has no decorator of its own: it is buy plus an "Adapt" annotation. Annotation 5 shows it on
// the CIB seven Tasklist variant: the bought Tasklist with our own form clarify-alternative.form.
// Database outsource (managed PostgreSQL) is an assumption: no hosting is decided yet.
// Products: Process engine = CIB seven, Process monitoring = CIB seven Cockpit,
// Application framework = Spring Boot, Database = PostgreSQL.
// Notes: green = Doctrine (talk colour legend); the uncoloured notes mark assumptions.
// Rationale, BPMN element ids and code per component: sourcing-decisions.md next to this file.
